  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Head it past your partner",
  "description": "Pairs with one ball and two small goals, or cone goals, facing each other 5–8 metres apart. With an odd number, make one group of three. Each player stands in a goal.\n\nTake turns to head for goal. Start by tossing the ball up to yourself and heading at your partner's goal while they try to save. Next step: your partner throws the ball to you and you head it straight at their goal. Each pair agrees which way to play and whether you may head a header straight back.\n\nAdjust the distance and goal size to how it goes. Count goals and compete within the pair, or hold a competition between all pairs. Variant: the same game with volleys instead of headers. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Keep your eyes open and watch the ball all the way onto your forehead."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Head with your forehead, not the top of your head."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Lean back and hit the ball with your upper body."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Head downwards – a bouncing header is hard to save."
    }
  ],
